<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- The Hermes seed's runtimes, signed under the Hardened Runtime by
       scripts/release.sh. Three entitlements, each measured as necessary
       on 2026-09-11 against the 0.3.17 release's own seed:

       allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory — Node (V8) cannot start
         without them: `node -e 1` dies with "Failed to reserve virtual
         memory for CodeRange". Node's own signature carries both; a
         re-sign without them removes them. That took out npm, npx,
         agent-browser (the browser lane's Chromium) and the WhatsApp bridge
         on every Mac that installed the release.

       disable-library-validation — Python under the Hardened Runtime refuses
         a native wheel signed by anyone else ("mapping process and mapped
         file have different Team IDs"). The seed's own wheels are re-signed
         beside it, so the seed runs; anything installed afterwards — a venv
         re-sync at a pin bump, `uv tool install browser-use`, pip — is
         ad-hoc signed and could not load, which is how the hermes-tools MCP
         server (pydantic_core) died and the brain ran with no tools.

       Nothing else: no audio, no Apple events — those are the app's, in
       Moe.entitlements. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
